  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-02-21T16:35:33.263Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Volumetric Lighting allows for lights to be visible as \"rays\", giving the illusion of \"God Rays\" and dust particles in the air which the light bounces off. This makes the map feel a lot warmer and gives it a lot more pop when set up correctly. \n\nThere's an Open Source script made by the Github user \"SlightyMad\" for this that's extremely easy to use. \nHere's a link to the Github page: https://github.com/SlightlyMad/VolumetricLights/\n\nAnd here is a YouTube video that shows just how easy it is to use: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=H5v_X1k02U0\n\nThough, this technique uses Deferred Rendering Path which is currently not usable in VRChat as far as I'm aware. Once this is enabled and the Volumetric Light script is whitelisted, it will enable world creators to easily create beautiful lighting with the correct setup.",
